    "INDEX-1<SEP>What are some good foods to eat when you are sick? I am looking for something to make my girlfriend to eat.<SEP>Sure, here are some good foods to eat when you are sick.\n1. Chicken noodle soup. The chicken in the soup provides protein and B vitamins, and the noodles are easy to digest. The broth can help thin mucus in your throat.\n2. Bananas. Bananas are rich in potassium and vitamin C, which can help maintain fluid balance and electrolytes. They are also easy to digest.\n3. Applesauce. Applesauce is easy to digest, and it is high in vitamin C, which can help boost your immune system. It is also a good source of fiber.\n4. White rice. White rice is easy to digest and can help replenish lost fluids and electrolytes. It is also a good source of carbohydrates for energy.\n5. Saltine crackers. Saltine crackers are easy to digest and can help replenish lost fluids and electrolytes. They are also a good source of carbohydrates for energy.": -4.8125,
